  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero, since no sure outcome exists), and the weighted mean differences — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not refer to any differences from a reference value or compute or compare such differences. Instead, the individual focuses exclusively on the probability of winning something (i.e., receiving a positive amount), which is unrelated to the mean difference from a reference value. The decision reason's rule — preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference — is not reflected in the justification. The individual’s reasoning is based on a different criterion (probability of non-zero outcome), not on the mean difference from a reference value. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not apply the rule of comparing weighted differences from zero to determine preference. Thus, the assessment is that the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
