  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — specifically, the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero, since no sure outcome exists), and the weighted mean of these differences — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention any calculation involving differences from zero or expected differences. Instead, they focus entirely on the probability of winning something, not on the expected value of the differences from zero. The decision reason requires evaluating the mean difference (which is the expected value in this case) and preferring the lottery with the more favorable one. Since both lotteries have the same expected value (6 Euros), the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not use the rule of comparing mean differences; they use a different criterion — maximizing the probability of a win. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual's justification is based on a different principle (probability of winning something), not on the mean difference from a reference value. Thus, the decision reason was not applied.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
