  "step_2": "The individual reports that they looked at both options and focused on the loss amounts and their probabilities. They mention calculating the expected losses. They state that they chose B because it has a lower expected loss. This indicates that the individual considered the expected value of the losses (i.e., the expected monetary outcome), and used that comparison to justify the choice. The deliberation process centers on comparing expected losses, which aligns with evaluating the expected value of each lottery. There is no mention of a reference value, differences from a reference, or any deviation from simply comparing expected values. The justification is straightforward: B has a lower expected loss, which matches the calculation of expected value. The individual did not mention differences from a reference value or any transformation of outcomes based on that reference, but since the reference value is zero in this case, the differences are just the outcomes themselves. Thus, the reasoning, while not explicitly mentioning the reference value or differences, effectively implements the same logic as the decision reason when the reference value is zero.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the outcomes, the reference value (zero), and the differences (outcomes themselves) weighted by probabilities — is present in the verbal report. The individual computes expected losses and chooses B because it has a lower expected loss. This is mathematically equivalent to the decision reason's rule when the reference value is zero. Although the individual does not explicitly mention the reference value or the concept of differences from a reference, their reasoning directly implements the same comparison: evaluating the expected value of the outcomes (which are negative) and selecting the one with the less negative expected value. Therefore, the individual used the decision reason in substance, even if not in explicit language. The justification matches the rule of the reason. Thus, the individual used the decision reason to make the decision.",
